WEBVTT

00:31.160 --> 00:33.030
In a future to come...

00:33.130 --> 00:37.860
the third energy revolution arrives
with the invention of the Shizuma Drive...

00:37.970 --> 00:40.960
and mankind reaches a
newfound period of prosperity.

00:41.870 --> 00:44.810
But within the shadows
of this bright peace...

00:44.910 --> 00:47.840
two powers clash against each other.

00:50.110 --> 00:54.240
A secret organization bent on
world domination, the BF Group!

00:56.820 --> 00:59.720
Everything for Big Fire!

01:18.540 --> 01:21.770
And to oppose this threat,
the Experts of Justice...

01:21.880 --> 01:24.740
is formed from members
gathered from all across the globe!

01:24.850 --> 01:26.710
The International Police Organization!

01:26.850 --> 01:31.510
With them is the most powerful
robot on the planet, Giant Robo...

01:31.650 --> 01:33.850
and the young man who commands it.

01:34.160 --> 01:36.420
His name is Daisaku Kusama!

01:38.290 --> 01:40.390
Crush them! Giant Robo!

01:47.000 --> 01:53.840
<i>GIANT ROBO</i>

01:53.940 --> 01:59.570
<i>THE DAY THE EARTH STOOD STILL</i>

02:04.750 --> 02:07.850
The new world's largest Shizuma
Power Plant, Saint Abbe...

02:07.960 --> 02:10.080
has steadily increased
its power output...

02:10.190 --> 02:12.290
and is scheduled to
reach 120% in three days.

02:12.390 --> 02:16.060
As planned, the plant will
generate 50% of the world's power.

02:16.160 --> 02:17.930
Now, Professor Shizuma, who disappeared...

02:18.030 --> 02:19.906
the day before the
opening of the power plant...

02:19.930 --> 02:23.740
still remains missing and concerns
for his safety have been raised.

02:34.050 --> 02:36.750
Oh, so it's finally been completed...

02:38.150 --> 02:40.880
Now that this has fallen into
the hands of the BF Group...

02:41.020 --> 02:43.620
I'm sure our long battle
will finally come to an end...

02:45.130 --> 02:47.220
Then let us begin the
operation immediately!

02:47.330 --> 02:49.520
No, we can't quite do that yet.

02:50.530 --> 02:52.560
What do you mean?

02:52.900 --> 02:56.130
It seems that our colleagues
are still in pursuit of the case.

02:56.470 --> 02:57.170
Then...

02:57.370 --> 02:59.970
There are two attache cases here...

03:00.340 --> 03:03.970
But there are three
samples that were prepared.

03:12.820 --> 03:15.310
In other words, the remaining case...

03:15.820 --> 03:17.380
is in the hands of our enemy.

03:33.740 --> 03:36.730
Where do you think you can
go at this point, Professor?

03:36.880 --> 03:39.580
Now, hand over the attache case!

03:40.320 --> 03:41.150
Don't be absurd!

03:41.250 --> 03:43.770
Do you know what would happen
to the world if I hand this over?

03:45.850 --> 03:50.150
All of this is because you developed
that drive system, isn't that right?

03:50.590 --> 03:54.090
That's exactly the reason! This
is my penance for what I've done!

03:55.730 --> 03:59.130
I see, but it's my duty
to recover that case.

04:00.240 --> 04:02.030
Oh God, please protect this case.

04:02.370 --> 04:05.530
If you're going to pray, you should pray
to the person you were ten years ago.

04:05.940 --> 04:06.940
Now then...

04:19.120 --> 04:19.880
Why you...

04:20.050 --> 04:21.750
This is no time to be surprised!

04:25.530 --> 04:26.620
The engine system!

04:41.610 --> 04:43.310
Now, Professor!

04:46.910 --> 04:49.410
Damn, we've entered into Nanking!

04:49.550 --> 04:50.680
Ginrei!

05:06.070 --> 05:07.540
Now! Jump!

05:15.780 --> 05:16.780
A woman?

05:33.260 --> 05:34.460
All right!

05:35.500 --> 05:36.860
How dare you!

05:37.500 --> 05:39.020
You won't get away!

05:40.200 --> 05:41.200
Launch!

05:53.610 --> 05:56.680
All Q Operatives have launched!

06:00.290 --> 06:03.550
Don't let them escape alive!
I don't care how, but get that case!

06:03.730 --> 06:04.730
Roger!

06:14.370 --> 06:15.100
Find them!

06:15.270 --> 06:16.910
They should be on the roof of that train!

06:23.510 --> 06:25.410
They got A! B will now assume command!

06:34.720 --> 06:35.720
There's no end to them!

06:38.930 --> 06:39.990
Leave it to me!

06:40.160 --> 06:41.160
Huh?

06:41.500 --> 06:44.800
No matter what happens,
don't use your powers!

06:44.900 --> 06:45.900
You got that?

06:46.670 --> 06:47.900
Come and get me!

06:48.300 --> 06:50.200
The Professor and the case are right here!

06:50.670 --> 06:53.800
Old man, hang on tight!

07:09.990 --> 07:12.650
<i>Kokushi Senpuu!</i>

07:21.340 --> 07:22.560
You bull-headed idiot!

07:26.310 --> 07:28.800
What if something had
happened to the Professor?

07:28.940 --> 07:30.310
Hurry up and bring him!

07:38.950 --> 07:40.320
Are you all right, Ginrei?

07:57.610 --> 07:59.130
Not this guy again!

07:59.370 --> 08:00.900
Give it up!

08:17.260 --> 08:19.630
So this thing was a BF robot?

08:20.190 --> 08:20.850
<i>Run!</i>

08:21.100 --> 08:22.100
<i>Faster!</i>

08:22.530 --> 08:24.560
Faster? Ya idiot!

08:25.000 --> 08:27.400
Who the hell is this?

08:31.270 --> 08:32.470
<i>Keep heading straight!</i>

08:57.160 --> 08:58.430
How dare you!

08:58.870 --> 09:00.460
You won't get away!

10:18.580 --> 10:20.070
T-That's...

10:24.650 --> 10:26.450
G-Giant Robo!

10:39.270 --> 10:45.800
E-Everything for Big Fire!

10:50.010 --> 10:51.170
Punch! Robo!

11:03.290 --> 11:05.490
How can this be?

11:19.970 --> 11:21.030
Ginrei!

11:21.240 --> 11:22.510
Tetsugyu!

11:22.940 --> 11:24.670
Please hang on tight!

11:24.910 --> 11:26.040
T-That's...

11:26.610 --> 11:27.980
Daisaku Kusama!

11:28.520 --> 11:29.810
And this is...

11:30.220 --> 11:31.550
Giant Robo!

11:33.620 --> 11:35.180
Robo! Rapid ascent!

11:56.580 --> 12:00.340
Thinking back on it now, this
was my first meeting with Daisaku...

12:01.150 --> 12:03.780
and the first day of that incident.

12:11.160 --> 12:16.120
Seven days that no one would ever forget...

12:23.400 --> 12:25.270
Giant Robo...

12:30.210 --> 12:32.610
The case has definitely
fallen into the enemy's hands...

12:36.750 --> 12:42.280
Perhaps it's time that we dealt
with that young boy named Daisaku.

12:43.760 --> 12:46.160
How the Magnificent Ten have fallen...

12:46.830 --> 12:50.760
Mr. Alberto, we still have
two of the samples in hand.

12:50.930 --> 12:55.160
Yes. With two, Giant
Robo is no threat to us.

12:56.770 --> 12:59.500
How dare you speak with such
insolence toward Master Alberto?

13:03.240 --> 13:04.240
Now, now...

13:04.280 --> 13:07.770
Let's not upset Ko Enshaku, who's
been sent here to observe us, shall we?

13:09.080 --> 13:11.350
My code name is Genya!

13:11.550 --> 13:15.180
As in the beautiful illusory night...

13:16.020 --> 13:18.520
You only need to remember that.

13:18.960 --> 13:19.960
Ivan!

13:20.060 --> 13:21.060
Sir!

13:23.060 --> 13:26.360
We will deal with the recovery
of the case at a later time.

13:26.700 --> 13:31.040
Let us proceed with our Still
Earth Operation as scheduled.

13:32.870 --> 13:36.470
Everything for Big Fire!

14:40.440 --> 14:42.810
Damn it! I'm too late!

14:45.380 --> 14:47.110
Your actions were in vain...

14:47.210 --> 14:51.410
Kenji Murasame of the International
Police Organization, Paris Branch...

14:51.520 --> 14:53.680
How could you perform such a heinous act?

14:59.930 --> 15:01.230
I-It can't be!

15:01.360 --> 15:02.360
You're...

15:02.830 --> 15:04.960
Professor Franken Von Vogler!

15:06.400 --> 15:07.530
It's revenge...

15:08.970 --> 15:10.800
P-Please wait, Professor!

15:19.080 --> 15:20.340
It's going out...

15:20.610 --> 15:23.980
The lights of Paris are
being extinguished...

15:50.410 --> 15:54.410
Those are the only images we can get
from the area using maximum magnification.

15:55.220 --> 15:58.010
What's going on here, Commander?

15:59.450 --> 16:03.910
Professor Go, will you tell
me your opinion as a scientist?

16:04.590 --> 16:05.220
Yes sir.

16:05.530 --> 16:08.460
The incident occurred
at 2400 hours Paris time.

16:08.760 --> 16:10.490
That would be 0600 hours here in Peking.

16:10.600 --> 16:13.620
It's been six hours since the land
around that area has risen like that.

16:13.730 --> 16:15.400
But without more data...

16:15.500 --> 16:17.630
I would like to refrain
from further comment.

16:18.110 --> 16:20.800
But one thing is for certain...

16:22.810 --> 16:25.486
Observe this footage taken from our
satellite that had begun monitoring...

16:25.510 --> 16:27.640
at the start of this incident.

16:30.450 --> 16:34.320
Starting from Notre Dame, which is at
the center of that newly formed tower...

16:34.420 --> 16:37.950
and expanding outward, every
Shizuma System has ceased to function.

16:38.130 --> 16:41.620
Everything runs on the
Shizuma Drive including...

16:41.800 --> 16:44.160
even the smallest items, like a lighter.

16:55.280 --> 16:56.800
That city is dead...

17:00.110 --> 17:01.580
The Shizuma Drive...

17:09.760 --> 17:14.060
Ten years ago, in a small
rural laboratory in Belgium...

17:14.960 --> 17:17.660
five scientists made a discovery.

17:18.670 --> 17:25.540
It was a clean and non-polluting
source of totally renewable energy.

17:29.040 --> 17:31.570
It was used on land, in
the skies and on the oceans.

17:32.780 --> 17:35.980
Used in times of peace and in war...

17:37.250 --> 17:39.580
In the factories, offices
and for the individual...

17:39.720 --> 17:43.680
Every conceivable use for
energy was transformed overnight...

17:43.960 --> 17:45.860
ending the depletion
of petroleum resources.

17:45.960 --> 17:48.620
Even the nuclear reactors
had begun to be dismantled.

17:49.430 --> 17:53.990
This power source is now as
common as air and water on this earth.

17:54.400 --> 17:58.340
It was given the name of its
inventor and called the Shizuma Drive.

17:58.710 --> 17:59.730
However...

18:01.010 --> 18:04.040
So you're saying that the
Shizuma Drive caused all this?

18:04.610 --> 18:06.270
Like what happened at Bashtarle?

18:07.450 --> 18:08.640
That's not possible!

18:09.250 --> 18:12.950
The Shizuma Drive is
a perfect energy system!

18:13.150 --> 18:14.310
It has to be!

18:20.790 --> 18:21.920
Uh, excuse me...

18:22.400 --> 18:23.400
I agree.

18:23.430 --> 18:24.960
The Shizuma is perfect.

18:25.370 --> 18:29.930
But that system is now being
threatened by an ominous shadow.

18:30.300 --> 18:33.300
That's what Notre Dame is proving to us.

18:37.640 --> 18:40.510
They are two of the scientists
that developed the Shizuma Drive!

18:41.280 --> 18:43.510
This is what Murasame was investigating.

18:43.680 --> 18:45.240
Hold on a second.

18:45.350 --> 18:49.480
What do those dead bodies have to do
with the suspension of the Shizuma Drive?

18:50.290 --> 18:51.350
Someone...

18:52.460 --> 18:54.860
No, most likely it's Big Fire...

18:56.200 --> 19:00.000
If he was trying to recreate
the "Tragedy of Bashtarle"...

19:03.340 --> 19:05.100
then they would be an obstacle.

19:06.170 --> 19:07.300
T-Then...

19:07.670 --> 19:10.010
It's too early to reach
any sort of conclusion...

19:10.580 --> 19:12.880
In any event, we have
the creator of the system...

19:12.980 --> 19:16.140
Professor Shizuma, under our protection.

19:16.250 --> 19:17.380
I'm sure he will be...

19:17.950 --> 19:19.650
coming...

19:20.020 --> 19:21.250
He's coming.

19:21.420 --> 19:22.720
He's coming.

19:35.770 --> 19:38.330
The Airship Greta Garbo
has reached Peking Base!

19:38.610 --> 19:40.630
Please begin the storage procedure of "G".

19:40.910 --> 19:41.910
Roger!

20:05.830 --> 20:07.960
First and secondary partitions in place!

20:08.440 --> 20:10.530
Legs locked in place! Condition green!

20:11.410 --> 20:12.500
Beginning maintenance!

20:14.110 --> 20:15.580
Retracting wire cables!

20:16.010 --> 20:17.710
Hurry up with the coolant tubes!

20:34.530 --> 20:36.330
Big brother!

20:40.430 --> 20:41.430
Welcome back!

20:42.270 --> 20:43.530
Big Brother!

20:43.900 --> 20:46.870
It looks like you got
back in one piece as well.

20:47.010 --> 20:50.380
How was your trip? You got
to be alone with Ginrei, right?

20:50.480 --> 20:51.480
Well?

20:56.380 --> 20:59.380
Anyways, it was a close one in Nanking!

20:59.890 --> 21:03.480
I thought you would be the
one to come and save us, but...

21:04.120 --> 21:06.120
instead that little brat comes!

21:15.140 --> 21:17.330
What was that? Who
were you calling a little brat?

21:17.470 --> 21:21.140
Who got his butt saved by that brat, again?

21:21.280 --> 21:22.710
Can you tell me?

21:26.680 --> 21:31.210
If you still have a complaint,
why not challenge him to a fight?

21:33.350 --> 21:36.410
Give me a break, Big Brother!

21:39.930 --> 21:41.760
Taiso! Tetsugyu!

21:42.030 --> 21:45.190
Even though we're back at the
base, our mission isn't over yet!

21:46.370 --> 21:50.130
What did you say, you little punk?

21:50.400 --> 21:52.340
Why I oughtta...

22:01.680 --> 22:02.680
Tetsugyu!

22:03.820 --> 22:08.620
Now, let's leave these children alone
and go make our report, shall we?

22:09.090 --> 22:10.090
Okay!

22:10.160 --> 22:12.090
Oh, come on!

22:17.130 --> 22:18.560
Welcome back.

22:19.200 --> 22:20.790
How did it go?

22:21.030 --> 22:23.370
Well, sir! The mission was completed!

22:24.370 --> 22:27.740
Professor Shizuma has
been taken to Medical, but...

22:27.840 --> 22:29.900
So he hasn't said anything since...

22:30.340 --> 22:31.340
No...

22:31.880 --> 22:38.010
But he did give me this to
give to you, Professor Go.

22:38.520 --> 22:40.890
Hey, we're the ones who got that...

22:41.360 --> 22:43.120
So this is the case...

22:48.660 --> 22:52.930
But what could Professor
Shizuma have been trying to get to us?

22:56.570 --> 22:57.570
This is...

22:58.970 --> 22:59.970
But it...

23:03.610 --> 23:07.710
So Daisaku, the Professor
hasn't said anything?

23:07.810 --> 23:08.810
No...

23:09.480 --> 23:11.280
except that once...

23:20.290 --> 23:21.290
Daisaku...

23:21.960 --> 23:26.760
I no longer have the courage... like
you have when you control Giant Robo...

23:26.930 --> 23:30.390
but I can't let something like
Bashtarle ever happen again...

23:36.340 --> 23:39.440
I didn't understand what
he was trying to say to me...

23:39.810 --> 23:40.970
Um, that's all right.

23:41.420 --> 23:43.540
Commander, can I have
a word with you later?

23:43.650 --> 23:44.650
Sure.

23:45.190 --> 23:46.780
Thank you, Daisaku.

23:46.950 --> 23:48.820
I'll take it from here.

23:49.290 --> 23:50.450
You've done well.

23:50.960 --> 23:52.390
We'll be counting on you.

23:52.490 --> 23:54.590
Please let Robo know that as well.

23:55.130 --> 23:57.060
Yes, thank you very much!

23:59.530 --> 24:02.660
Ginrei, please submit the
final mission report to me.

24:02.840 --> 24:03.360
Yes sir.

24:03.470 --> 24:04.470
Then, dismissed!

24:04.640 --> 24:05.640
Yes, sir!

24:09.540 --> 24:10.570
How is he?

24:10.680 --> 24:12.010
It's hard to say.

24:12.180 --> 24:13.840
He hasn't said anything really...

24:14.050 --> 24:17.310
Although he occasionally mumbles
about something, but I can't make it out.

24:19.490 --> 24:20.490
I see.

24:23.190 --> 24:24.950
V-Vogler is coming...

24:25.390 --> 24:27.520
Vogler is coming...

24:29.400 --> 24:30.460
He's coming...

24:30.700 --> 24:31.760
He's coming...

24:32.270 --> 24:34.390
Vogler is coming!

24:45.550 --> 24:46.550
Wow!

25:19.250 --> 25:20.480
Enthusiastic, aren't you?

25:23.680 --> 25:26.050
Do you like the Shizuma Drive?

25:26.220 --> 25:27.980
I think it's amazing!

25:28.560 --> 25:33.120
That little cylinder can power anything
from radios to cars and airplanes!

25:33.390 --> 25:36.420
And unlike the batteries up until
now, it's completely renewable!

25:36.600 --> 25:37.600
I agree.

25:37.760 --> 25:42.360
We no longer have to worry about depleting
our oil resources or air pollution.

25:42.800 --> 25:44.030
That's true!

25:44.600 --> 25:47.010
Being able to rescue the
Professor who invented...

25:47.110 --> 25:49.670
this super energy
source is such an honor!

25:50.780 --> 25:52.300
It makes me really happy!

25:52.750 --> 25:58.280
Yes, everything resulted from
Professor Shizuma inventing this system...

26:01.020 --> 26:03.460
Hey Ginrei!

26:07.890 --> 26:08.690
Yo!

26:08.900 --> 26:13.830
Now that the mission is finally
over, what say we go and celebrate!

26:13.970 --> 26:15.830
What do you think, Daisaku?

26:15.940 --> 26:18.630
You're twelve now, right?

26:19.070 --> 26:21.970
Wanna go someplace
"special" for this occasion?

26:22.080 --> 26:23.240
What do you say?

26:23.340 --> 26:24.340
Um...

26:25.180 --> 26:26.480
No, it's okay...

26:27.680 --> 26:29.120
Don't do it, Daisaku.

26:30.120 --> 26:31.920
You'll wind up growing
up into a bad adult...

26:31.950 --> 26:35.050
if you hang around hopeless
people like them too much!

26:35.690 --> 26:37.060
What do you mean, "hopeless"?

26:37.160 --> 26:38.460
A "bad adult"?

26:45.300 --> 26:46.460
That's right!

26:47.070 --> 26:50.870
Daisaku is going out
on a date with me, right?

26:51.200 --> 26:53.170
What?

27:07.620 --> 27:09.920
D-D-D-Date?

27:10.190 --> 27:11.190
That's right!

27:11.420 --> 27:12.420
Um, it's all right!

27:13.590 --> 27:15.360
Hey, where're you going?

27:15.700 --> 27:17.320
To help with the maintenance!

27:17.430 --> 27:18.760
Robo is waiting for me!

27:24.840 --> 27:25.900
Oh gee...

27:26.310 --> 27:27.470
Looks like I got dumped...

27:27.570 --> 27:28.570
Um...

27:30.140 --> 27:31.770
If it's okay with you...

27:31.040 --> 27:32.040
<i>Yes?</i>

27:32.350 --> 27:35.540
D-D-Date...

27:36.620 --> 27:37.520
Go ahead.

27:37.620 --> 27:40.820
Take Taiso and go somewhere
"special" or whatever...

27:44.860 --> 27:45.860
Man...

27:48.830 --> 27:49.850
Shall we, then?

27:58.570 --> 28:01.870
Professor Go, there are now three bodies...

28:02.580 --> 28:04.810
The only one remaining
is Professor Shizuma...

28:04.910 --> 28:06.640
There's one more thing...

28:07.010 --> 28:09.480
according to the reconnaissance
data we just received...

28:09.650 --> 28:12.780
there is some kind of large
metallic object that was detected...

28:13.120 --> 28:16.060
500 meters beneath Notre Dame.

28:18.260 --> 28:21.490
What's peculiar is that the large
chamber containing the metallic object...

28:21.700 --> 28:25.150
is showing indications that some
kind of power is being generated there.

28:25.270 --> 28:27.760
So then it's safe to
assume that what ever it is...

28:27.870 --> 28:30.430
it must be causing all the
Shizuma Drives to stop working.

28:30.800 --> 28:33.360
But if so, then why haven't
they proceeded further?

28:33.640 --> 28:36.740
They probably need this...

28:49.560 --> 28:53.460
So this is the legacy of what
happened ten years ago...

28:53.660 --> 28:55.220
No doubt about it.

28:55.700 --> 28:59.860
No one besides him could make this.

29:00.530 --> 29:05.900
Then, are you saying that Professor
Franken Von Vogler survived the tragedy?

29:06.010 --> 29:07.270
That's not possible!

29:07.770 --> 29:08.770
No...

29:09.010 --> 29:10.270
It can't be...

29:12.750 --> 29:16.340
I'm sure that Professor Vogler is...

29:21.990 --> 29:25.580
Then who... and for what reason?

29:26.590 --> 29:27.720
I don't know...

29:27.990 --> 29:31.120
But if all three were to
be brought together...

29:31.230 --> 29:33.460
then the tragedy of
Bashtarle would be repeated.

30:14.440 --> 30:18.900
The future has given the light
of glory to the men of the present!

30:19.010 --> 30:24.080
Yes, the time has finally come
when we will conquer all our fears!

30:24.620 --> 30:27.610
Ancient man rubbed together
pieces of wood to create fire!

30:27.720 --> 30:33.350
For oil, men once fought and killed the whale,
and later they fought and killed each other!

30:33.530 --> 30:38.160
Then came nuclear power! In every age,
we lived with such dangers all around us!

30:38.670 --> 30:40.500
But now it will be different!

30:40.670 --> 30:44.540
We no longer need to fear!
The night is finally ours!

30:45.470 --> 30:48.410
This time for certain, we
will have our beautiful night!

30:48.640 --> 30:50.540
This is not an illusion!

30:55.920 --> 30:59.150
We can't leave things
to the Professor anymore!

30:59.290 --> 31:00.810
That's right, we have to stop him!

31:00.920 --> 31:02.860
Stop Vogler!

31:03.160 --> 31:04.750
He's out of control!

31:04.960 --> 31:07.860
Pull him away! Don't let him get near it!

31:08.390 --> 31:10.090
Was this all for nothing?

31:10.200 --> 31:10.890
That's right!

31:11.000 --> 31:13.090
The experiment isn't ready!

31:13.270 --> 31:14.560
It's too dangerous!

31:15.600 --> 31:16.600
It's too late!

31:19.910 --> 31:22.540
I have lived by this,
and I will die by it as well!

31:22.740 --> 31:25.010
What reason is there to hesitate?

31:25.110 --> 31:27.880
We have to abandon the lab!

31:27.980 --> 31:28.810
Do as you will!

31:28.920 --> 31:31.580
None of you have the right to
become creators of the night!

31:31.920 --> 31:33.580
But I can see it!

31:33.790 --> 31:35.350
I can see the beautiful night!

31:40.190 --> 31:42.190
I made you this promise!

31:43.030 --> 31:44.590
One day soon...

31:45.130 --> 31:49.230
I shall deliver the
beautiful night to all people!

31:49.670 --> 31:53.970
So that they may face their
fear of the night and win!

32:37.050 --> 32:39.040
The beautiful night...

32:39.590 --> 32:41.610
The beautiful night...

32:42.390 --> 32:43.520
One day...

32:43.820 --> 32:44.920
Once again...

32:45.090 --> 32:46.120
I will...

32:46.730 --> 32:48.060
I will...

33:21.660 --> 33:22.720
Stop it!

33:43.250 --> 33:44.250
What is it?

33:44.420 --> 33:46.940
Sir, I'm sorry to disturb you.

33:47.050 --> 33:50.350
Regarding last night's incident with
the Experts of Justice, unfortunately...

33:50.520 --> 33:51.220
I see...

33:51.320 --> 33:53.730
So, Master Alberto has already left.

33:53.860 --> 33:55.490
I see. I'll be right there.

34:48.980 --> 34:50.140
My god...

34:50.280 --> 34:52.120
How were they able to make such a base?

34:52.720 --> 34:55.420
This will certainly bring
shame to the Paris Branch...

34:58.990 --> 35:01.830
Master Alberto should
be reaching Peking shortly.

35:02.030 --> 35:05.560
Just tell him to eliminate
Professor Shizuma when he locates him!

35:06.100 --> 35:08.530
And to recover the
case as soon as possible!

35:08.630 --> 35:10.540
Vogler is waiting...

35:11.440 --> 35:13.740
What? Vogler?

35:17.080 --> 35:20.670
Then Professor Vogler is still...

35:38.870 --> 35:40.090
Soon...

35:41.930 --> 35:45.370
Very soon, I will finish
what began ten years ago...

36:23.340 --> 36:25.070
Will this do, sir?

36:29.420 --> 36:30.420
Yes.

36:42.260 --> 36:43.660
Professor Shizuma...

36:48.670 --> 36:52.540
and the Tragedy of
Bashtarle. Survivors...

36:53.710 --> 36:54.710
none.

36:59.010 --> 37:00.270
It can't be...

37:00.580 --> 37:01.580
Master Alberto...

37:02.050 --> 37:04.880
What is it? We haven't moved in a while...

37:04.980 --> 37:05.680
Well...

37:05.890 --> 37:08.696
It seems that traffic is being held
up by a couple of drunks in the road.

37:08.720 --> 37:12.450
This is why I don't
enjoy cities such as this.

37:12.690 --> 37:14.320
It's all right. I'll get out here.

37:14.690 --> 37:17.690
Then I shall wait for you over there.

37:23.040 --> 37:27.230
Bring more booze!

37:28.310 --> 37:30.710
I'm sorry about the ruckus.

37:30.810 --> 37:31.810
You idiot!

37:31.880 --> 37:33.510
What's that, Big Brother?

37:33.610 --> 37:34.510
Another bar?

37:34.610 --> 37:35.670
Sounds good to me!

37:35.850 --> 37:39.050
I'll follow you wherever you go!

37:40.120 --> 37:42.550
You fool! You're making
too much of a scene!

37:49.930 --> 37:50.930
Oh, you idiot!

37:51.000 --> 37:53.830
<i>Doh Shu Restaurant</i>

38:02.340 --> 38:04.830
Giant Robo my butt!

38:05.880 --> 38:08.780
It's just an old piece of junk!

38:08.880 --> 38:13.320
And the brat can't do a thing without it!

38:14.220 --> 38:19.780
That damned kid acts like he's
taking on the BF Group all by himself!

38:21.630 --> 38:24.220
What's the matter with you today, Tetsugyu?

38:24.430 --> 38:25.590
I don't like it!

38:25.730 --> 38:27.290
I don't like it at all!

38:29.440 --> 38:34.200
What, so you don't like Daisaku
and Ginrei getting friendly then?

38:34.570 --> 38:36.010
T-That's not it!

38:36.510 --> 38:38.880
Heh, that's it, isn't it?

38:42.780 --> 38:44.340
More booze!

38:44.450 --> 38:46.680
Bring more booze!

38:50.090 --> 38:52.960
But Big Brother, in this last mission...

38:53.060 --> 38:57.050
Ginrei and I worked
hard to get that case...

38:58.100 --> 39:05.200
But he handed it over to the
Commander like he got it all on his own!

39:12.650 --> 39:15.950
I mean, what about all the men
who died during the mission...

39:16.050 --> 39:17.570
What about them?

39:19.150 --> 39:20.640
What about them?

39:21.620 --> 39:25.750
Tetsugyu, we're Experts of Justice, right?

39:28.290 --> 39:29.520
Here's your order!

39:33.800 --> 39:37.740
Listen, Daisaku is still only
a child. He's twelve years old!

39:38.240 --> 39:42.440
Think about it, where were we at that age?

39:43.140 --> 39:46.510
It was about the time we
were recruited, I guess.

39:47.650 --> 39:48.650
That's right.

39:48.780 --> 39:50.840
It was around the time we first met.

39:51.280 --> 39:54.980
But could we do then,
what Daisaku has to do now?

39:56.390 --> 40:00.050
We chose the training to
become Experts of Justice.

40:00.460 --> 40:03.690
That's why we can do whatever it
takes to complete our missions...

40:04.200 --> 40:06.930
and with it, we can
face death if need be.

40:08.000 --> 40:10.600
But Daisaku suddenly found
himself shouldered with the...

40:10.840 --> 40:13.720
responsibility of commanding the
most powerful robot on the planet...

40:14.070 --> 40:17.940
and without any training, he was
given the duty of an Expert of Justice.

40:18.940 --> 40:21.610
Without warning, everything
was just thrust into his hands!

40:22.280 --> 40:25.720
Could we have handled
that when we were twelve?

40:31.720 --> 40:34.090
His first memories are of...

40:34.360 --> 40:38.990
his father being killed by the BF
Group and leaving him with Giant Robo.

40:39.970 --> 40:43.060
What are we supposed
to do for a kid like that?

40:45.100 --> 40:45.870
That's right...

40:45.970 --> 40:47.000
Nothing!

40:48.310 --> 40:53.800
The only thing we can do is to
ensure that he grows into a proper adult.

40:54.210 --> 40:55.240
That's it.

40:57.620 --> 40:58.850
But Big Brother...

40:59.490 --> 41:01.450
by the time I was twelve...

41:02.120 --> 41:03.820
I'd already killed a man.

41:14.030 --> 41:14.520
Big Brother!

41:14.930 --> 41:15.930
Yeah!

41:29.250 --> 41:30.550
What's going on?

41:39.190 --> 41:40.320
This way! Over here!

41:42.660 --> 41:44.150
Did you locate him?

41:44.300 --> 41:45.390
D-13 Block!

41:45.760 --> 41:47.200
This is E-6, it's all clear!

41:47.330 --> 41:48.360
D-2 Block is in ruins!

41:48.530 --> 41:49.730
He's headed for A-3!

41:49.940 --> 41:50.940
There he is!

42:05.890 --> 42:06.890
What's the matter?

42:06.950 --> 42:09.010
Can't you even put up a decent fight?

42:09.190 --> 42:13.390
I heard that this base houses
the finest of your organization!

42:19.330 --> 42:21.230
Aren't you the busy one?

42:21.370 --> 42:23.500
If you're here, why don't you be useful?

42:27.670 --> 42:29.110
There are now two enemies!

42:32.710 --> 42:34.010
Alberto the Impact...

42:35.410 --> 42:37.850
Then the Magnificent Ten is on the move?

42:38.250 --> 42:39.490
Where are Taiso and the others?

42:39.790 --> 42:42.220
I've put out the call signs,
but they haven't responded!

42:44.760 --> 42:48.560
Commander, their goal is obvious.

42:48.890 --> 42:50.990
Then it can't be helped,
I'm counting on you!

42:52.630 --> 42:53.630
Ginrei.

42:53.730 --> 42:54.730
Yes, sir!

42:55.170 --> 42:56.170
What?

42:59.940 --> 43:02.140
Where are Taiso and
Tetsugyu at a time like this!?

43:04.140 --> 43:05.140
Hurry!

43:05.840 --> 43:06.840
Daisaku!

43:09.780 --> 43:11.340
Quickly, over here!

43:16.420 --> 43:17.420
Hurry!

43:20.930 --> 43:21.930
Go!

43:33.040 --> 43:34.060
There they are!

43:41.610 --> 43:42.740
You'll not get away!

43:55.830 --> 43:56.830
Here he comes!

44:14.580 --> 44:15.710
Iron Fans!

44:21.090 --> 44:22.420
Professor Go, you did it!

44:25.490 --> 44:26.820
How quaint.

44:50.680 --> 44:51.680
It's over!

44:52.050 --> 44:53.050
Daisaku!

44:56.220 --> 44:57.220
What?

45:04.330 --> 45:05.700
You!

45:10.040 --> 45:11.300
Taiso...

45:12.200 --> 45:14.640
Tetsugyu, you go with the
Professor and the others.

45:14.940 --> 45:15.570
All right.

45:15.810 --> 45:16.940
What about you, Big Brother?

45:17.310 --> 45:20.470
I can handle them on my own.

45:21.050 --> 45:22.070
Taiso!

45:31.190 --> 45:32.920
Ginrei, go!

45:33.060 --> 45:34.060
Huh?

45:34.190 --> 45:35.190
Okay!

45:39.230 --> 45:40.860
So, Alberto...

45:41.230 --> 45:44.000
Looks like you had a bit of
fun while I was out, did you?

45:46.240 --> 45:49.970
How perfect! We can settle
the score from our last encounter.

45:50.740 --> 45:52.770
The score might be a bit too high for you!

46:27.750 --> 46:28.840
Oh no! The Peking Base!

46:28.950 --> 46:30.640
Shut up! It'll be fine!

46:30.920 --> 46:33.350
Brother Taiso will handle it!

46:33.650 --> 46:34.850
But Robo is...

46:35.090 --> 46:36.180
He'll be okay!

46:36.290 --> 46:39.280
He's stored beneath
an old nuclear reactor...

46:39.460 --> 46:43.620
so even the Magnificent Ten
will have a hard time getting to it!

46:43.930 --> 46:47.890
That's right. We have to rendezvous
with the Greta Garbo as soon as possible!

46:48.000 --> 46:48.630
All right!

46:48.930 --> 46:51.700
Professor Go, where are
we going with the Greta?

46:52.940 --> 46:55.416
We're heading to the main
headquarters of the Experts of Justice...

46:55.440 --> 46:56.930
To Ryozanpaku in the south!

46:57.740 --> 47:01.040
There, I'll determine the true
nature of the contents of this case!

47:01.910 --> 47:03.850
Is that all right with you, Professor?

47:09.690 --> 47:11.660
The true nature?

47:11.760 --> 47:14.420
Isn't that just a normal Shizuma cylinder?

47:14.730 --> 47:16.390
No, it's not!

47:16.730 --> 47:18.060
Little punk...

47:20.670 --> 47:22.000
Take a good look.

47:22.170 --> 47:24.330
This isn't an ordinary Shizuma cylinder!

47:24.700 --> 47:25.830
You're right...

47:28.770 --> 47:31.300
But what's this got to do with anything?

47:32.980 --> 47:36.440
This is the source of everything
that's happening now...

47:36.720 --> 47:42.310
Yes, it's just like the Tragedy
of Bashtarle ten years ago!

47:42.720 --> 47:43.720
What?

47:43.920 --> 47:45.410
It can't be...

47:45.990 --> 47:48.860
So that the same
mistakes aren't repeated...

47:49.030 --> 47:51.390
please tell us the truth
behind this Shizuma cylinder!

47:52.460 --> 47:53.120
Professor!

47:53.400 --> 47:57.530
Are you willing to let the Tragedy of
Bashtarle happen all over again?

47:57.770 --> 47:58.770
Professor!

48:03.580 --> 48:04.270
Let me go!

48:04.380 --> 48:05.840
Let me go! What are you doing?

48:07.610 --> 48:10.810
Professor, you're the only
one who can put a stop to this!

48:11.120 --> 48:12.120
It's too late!

48:12.380 --> 48:15.790
I have lived by this,
and I will die by it as well!

48:15.950 --> 48:18.290
What reason is there to hesitate?

48:18.560 --> 48:19.620
Professor!

48:20.390 --> 48:24.730
One day, the beautiful
night will come once again...

48:27.530 --> 48:31.470
None of you have the right to
become the creators of the night!

48:31.740 --> 48:33.570
of the night!

48:34.270 --> 48:36.140
of the night!

48:37.610 --> 48:38.610
The night!

48:44.080 --> 48:45.080
I'm sorry!

48:50.720 --> 48:51.720
I'm sorry!

48:52.960 --> 48:54.360
I'm sorry!

48:54.590 --> 48:57.320
Go, I'll talk!

48:57.600 --> 48:59.260
So, please save me!

48:59.560 --> 49:01.620
Please! I've had enough!

49:01.970 --> 49:05.600
I should never have
created the Shizuma Drive!

49:06.100 --> 49:07.870
How could you say that, Professor?

49:08.440 --> 49:10.380
The Shizuma Drive is a fabulous invention!

49:12.040 --> 49:15.380
Please, protect me from Vogler!

49:15.950 --> 49:16.950
Vogler?

49:17.050 --> 49:20.280
Then Professor Franken
Von Vogler is still...

49:20.420 --> 49:23.120
That's enough of that talk!

49:29.430 --> 49:30.430
It's...

49:30.500 --> 49:32.090
A BF Group robot!

49:41.940 --> 49:45.880
Now, hand over that case!
Along with the Professor, if you will!

50:04.030 --> 50:07.230
An evacuation order is in effect! Quickly
dispose of sensitive materials, and...

50:07.670 --> 50:11.130
What's the matter? Hurry up and move
Robo to the surface and evacuate!

50:11.300 --> 50:12.300
But...

50:18.040 --> 50:19.410
Robo is trying to launch?

50:19.510 --> 50:22.610
But Daisaku hasn't sent a call sign!

50:34.090 --> 50:36.530
Amazing! The power output is
fifty times greater than normal!

50:37.160 --> 50:39.760
Could it be that Robo
has an Auto Guard Circuit...

50:39.870 --> 50:42.230
that can detect a threat
to the life of the operator?

50:56.950 --> 50:57.750
Robo?

50:57.880 --> 50:58.880
Could it be that...

51:03.520 --> 51:06.190
Taiso, you should pay more attention!

51:07.330 --> 51:08.330
Now die!

51:12.700 --> 51:14.960
<i>Did something happen to Daisaku?</i>

51:20.570 --> 51:26.530
<i>EPISODE ONE, THE BLACK ATTACHE CASE
THE END</i>

51:26.910 --> 51:28.710
Things look desperate for our heroes!

51:29.110 --> 51:31.050
The base has been overrun...

51:31.150 --> 51:35.090
the BF Group Robot, Uranus,
closes in on Daisaku and the others!

51:35.850 --> 51:39.880
Will the black attache case once
again fall into the hands of the BF Group?

51:40.790 --> 51:43.420
What was the Tragedy of Bashtarle?

51:44.560 --> 51:46.690
And what is the Still Earth Operation?

51:47.230 --> 51:49.260
Within the multiple spirals of mysteries...

51:49.430 --> 51:52.170
the true identity of
Vogler becomes clear!

52:37.250 --> 52:41.210
No doubt about it, this is the same as
it was with the Tragedy of Bashtarle...

52:43.360 --> 52:44.620
It's beautiful...

52:45.120 --> 52:46.650
The beautiful night...

52:47.490 --> 52:51.220
but man always forgets
the filthy incidents of the past.

52:51.830 --> 52:54.300
Who do you think is responsible for it all?

52:55.170 --> 53:00.730
I'll make you remember!
Remember the true night!

53:05.310 --> 53:10.150
<i>TO BE CONTINUED</i>
